      "text": "Korean media report that Micron has received its first piece of production equipment at its HBM packaging plant in Singapore and expects to begin initial production in early 2027.\n\nThe first tool to arrive was a thermocompression (TC) bonder from Hanmi Semiconductor for HBM production. Total investment in the project is reportedly $7 billion.\n\nIndustry estimates put Micron’s HBM production capacity at around 100,000 wafer starts per month by the end of 2026, nearly double the level a year earlier.\n\nOn a wafer-start basis, Micron is still at roughly half the level of Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix. Its capacity is expected to grow as more packaging equipment arrives at key sites in Singapore and Taiwan.\n\n$MU",
